                {
                    "question": "Why does nigiri rice taste different from regular rice?",
                    "answer": "The rice is seasoned right after cooking with a mix of rice vinegar, sugar, and salt, then fanned to cool it to room temperature, which gives it a slightly tangy flavor and glossy texture.",
                },
                {
                    "question": "Should you dip nigiri in soy sauce rice-side or fish-side?",
                    "answer": "Fish-side down. Dipping the rice causes it to absorb too much sauce and fall apart, and it oversalts the piece compared to dipping just the topping.",
                },
